Title: The Wedding
Order: 8
Production Code: 1x08

INT. TELEGRAPH OFFICE - NIGHT

SFX: a telegraph key clattering

[[Aubrey Livingston]], alone, dictates a wire.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(dictating)
"To Jim Titus, Laurel Hill, Virginia. Be on hand at the New York dock, first of the month. I will be there to make things right for you. Ten thousand if you succeed the first six months. A.L."

He folds the receipt away like it costs him nothing.

INT. VANCE ESTATE - HALL - DAY (THE NEXT MORNING)

AMB: a house full of well-wishers

[[Reuel Briggs]] and [[Dianthe Lusk]] stand married, hands clasped, saying goodbye at the door.

DIANTHE LUSK
If you knew how weak I am, you wouldn't leave me.

REUEL BRIGGS
I wish to God I could take you with me.

He kisses her, and she is still smiling through tears as he goes.

EXT. NEW YORK DOCK - DAY

AMB: gulls, a ship's horn, dockside noise

[[Reuel Briggs]], [[Charlie Vance]], and their newly hired manservant [[Jim Titus]] board the Liverpool steamer.

INT. BAR HARBOR - MUSIC ROOM - NIGHT (LATER)

AMB: a summer house party, a waltz just ending

Weeks later, at a house party, [[Dianthe Lusk]] rises unbidden and sits at the piano, playing and singing as if compelled.

DIANTHE LUSK
(singing, trance-like)
Go down, Moses, way down in Egypt's land —

A second voice, a contralto, seems to answer hers from nowhere in the room. Every guest goes still. She finishes and faints dead away.

Later, alone with her in the library, [[Aubrey Livingston]] finally tells her the truth of who she was — and what she is.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
There is rest and security in my love, Dianthe. I have learned to love you. I am prepared to save you from what must be your fate if Reuel ever learns your origin.

DIANTHE LUSK
(recoiling)
You would have me give up everything — for you?

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
I give you a week to think it over.

She sinks to her knees, and says nothing more.
